# Workflow Phases Router

Canon: `AGENTS.md` § Session phases. Detail: `docs/agent-workflows/workflow-phases.md`.

## Phase order (Normal+)

```text
align → contract → slice → implement → verify → STOPPED_AT_APPROVED_SCOPE
```

## HITL vs AFK

**HITL:** ambiguous intent · contract create/amend · slice shape review · merge approval · taste/UX/domain judgment

**AFK:** implement against explicit contract · bounded refactor · verification with explicit commands

Do not convert HITL work into AFK because a plan file exists.

## Vertical slice

Prefer tracer-bullet slices over horizontal phases. Valid slice: crosses relevant boundary end-to-end · runnable feedback in same PR · independently reviewable.

Reject or rewrite plans that are only schema-only, DTO-only, serializer-only, UI-only, or "foundation" without runnable feedback — unless user explicitly scoped **infra-only**.

## Fresh-context review

After Normal+ implementation: new session or review subagent. Re-read contract/acceptance · inspect diff · run smallest validation · escalate to `quality-check` / `bugbot-policy.mdc` for boundary risk.

## plan-run metadata

Plans should include `slice_type`, `afk_eligible`, `blocked_by` (see `plan-run` skill § Plan frontmatter contract).

`plan-run auto` only when `afk_eligible: true`, clean worktree, explicit contract/acceptance/stop.

## Alignment skill

Ambiguous features: `/grill-me-shapez2` before contract (`grill-me-shapez2` skill).

## Kanban

Normal+ tasks: one `.devtool/features/` card per thread; update on phase change (`kanban-tracking.mdc`).
